D7D7AF][/dim]Typing `%m:` / `%model:` shows model aliases as unmistakable, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]richly annotated rows beneath the concrete model names, each [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]showing what it resolves to and how it was configured, and typing [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`@` after the colon narrows the menu to aliases only — in the ACE [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]prompt input and in editors through the xprompt LSP.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]model_alias_completion.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-ao[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix the `@` alias gate in the prompt-input directive grammar[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]gate[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]gate: make a leading `@` in a `%model:` value stay in model-argument [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]context instead of being read as an `@effort` suffix, matching the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]already-correct sase-core grammar.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Enrich the model completion catalog with alias resolution and [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]provenance[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog: derive alias rows from the same AliasView data the Models panel[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]uses, add a read-only temporary-override peek, split the catalog into a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]config-token-cached static build plus a cheap override overlay, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extend the LSP catalog JSON additively.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render alias rows in the ACE completion panel[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rows[dim] · [dim][/dim]after gate, catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows: add a shared model-alias presentation module used by both the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Models panel and the completion menu, render `%model` values as an [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]aligned four-column grid with alias kind badges and resolution badges, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add the contextual panel title/subtitle, and warm the catalog off the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keystroke path.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Surface the alias detail through the xprompt LSP[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lsp[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lsp: consume the new catalog fields in sase-core's xprompt LSP so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]editors show alias kind, resolution target, provenance, and description,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with stable model-before-alias ordering.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Visual snapshots, docs, and help text[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after rows, lsp[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]polish: add ACE PNG snapshots for the mixed and alias-only menus, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update the xprompt/LLM docs plus the ACE help popup to describe the `@` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]alias gate.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ao","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-ao.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-5ef1cc7cf6f3588b9b147c5138e7426f","started_at":"2026-07-29T11:47:29.177641+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"9c6e2aef2f9f8db31debb1f7d64f78573d58cef42813eb6ef9cfa2bd4a9e7d11","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ao.5/commits.json","size_bytes